File Index

/package.json
Purpose: @shatteredarchive/psd-viewer-server manifest — deps ag-psd + pngjs + express + cors; dev/start set --max-old-space-size=8192 for large composites.

/tsconfig.json
Purpose: NodeNext ESM build config extending the repo base; emits to dist/.

/README.md
Purpose: What the service does, the endpoint table, the local-first security caveat, and how to run it.

/src/index.ts
Purpose: The whole service — initializeCanvas ImageData shim (no native canvas), /health, /api/presets (the ~/Downloads sample PSDs that exist), and /api/psd/png which decodes the composite only (ag-psd skipLayerImageData + useImageData) and streams a pngjs-encoded PNG with X-Psd-Width/Height/X-Decode-Ms headers. 2026-07-29 (CodeQL path-injection): ?path= no longer reaches the filesystem raw. resolveInsideRoot() is the single chokepoint (same idiom as mud-builder-server's area-store.areaFilePath): resolve against PSD_ROOT = ~/Downloads, require a .psd extension, reject anything not contained by the root, and re-check via realpathSync so an in-root symlink pointing out is not an escape hatch — refused with 403 BEFORE any fs call, so an out-of-root path isn't even an existence oracle. A relative value resolves against the root, so a bare "Princess.psd" still works. Comparison is case-folded on win32 (a hand-typed c:\users\... must match a C:\Users\... root). Bare cors() also replaced by a localhost:62080 dev-origin allowlist that still permits ORIGINLESS requests, since the normal path is vite's server-side proxy hop, not a browser cross-origin call. Be precise about the split: containment is what bounds what can be read at all; CORS only stops a hostile page READING the response, because a plain cross-origin GET isn't preflighted and still executes. Runtime-verified: traversal/absolute-outside/non-psd all 403, missing in-root .psd 404, evil Origin gets no ACAO header, and a real 3525x5000 Princess.psd still decodes to an 18.7MB PNG.
